          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "गारा (gārā) may come from Sanskrit karaka, \"hail\", as a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. CDIAL lists it under karaka but marks the Marathi word with a query, so the link is possible rather than certain (CDIAL 2782). Gujarati karā, \"hail\", sits in the same entry without one."
            }
          ]
        },
